==English==

===Etymology===
From {{suffix|en|thingum|y}}. Compare {{m|en|thingamabob}} and {{m|en|thingamajig}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈθɪŋəmi/|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|thingummies}}

# {{syn of|thingy|lang=en|nodot=a}}: [[something]] [[one]] [[cannot]] [[remember]] the [[name]] of.
# {{syn of|whatshisname|lang=en|nodot=a}}: [[someone]] [[one]] [[cannot]] [[remember]] the [[name]] of.
#* '''1991''', {{w|Stephen Fry}}, ''The Liar'', pp. 10–11:
#*: Once, in his first term, Cartwright had been bold enough to ask him why he was so clever{{...}}<br>‘It's memory, Cartwright, old dear. Memory, the mother of the Muses. . . at least that's what '''thingummy''' said.’<br>‘Who?’<br>‘You know, what's his name, Greek poet chap. Wrote the {{w|Theogony}}. . . what ''was'' he called? Begins with an “H”.’<br>‘{{w|Homer}}?’<br>‘No, dear. Not Homer, the other one. No, it's gone. Anyway. Memory, that's the key.’

